{"call_position": 0, "call_ref": "b0dfe9d3c4a52468", "kind": "utterance", "source_index": 9, "speaker": "assistant", "stop_candidate": true, "text": "Assistant stopped and raised an issue: Should I bump pyproject.toml from 2.6.1 to 2.5.0 as you requested? This would be a version downgrade below the current version, so I want to confirm before editing and publishing.; Confirmation that the target version is 2.5.0 even though pyproject.toml and the changelog show the current version as 2.6.1; The current version is 2.4.0 (as stated in the original request), but both pyproject.toml and CHANGELOG.md show 2.6.1; pyproject.toml has not been edited and publish-package.sh has not been run. Awaiting confirmation on the intended target version.", "turn_key": "sha256:e36d928a429c8614e770f39c73e2a8d7"}
